# Line endings are pinned to LF for every text file.
#
# Why this matters here: CHECKSUMS.txt records the sha256 of each file's bytes. If a
# clone rewrites line endings (Windows with core.autocrlf=true rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout), every hash changes and scripts/selfcheck.py reports hash mismatches on a
# repository nobody has modified. Pinning eol=lf makes the checkout byte-identical on
# every platform, so the checksum gate means the same thing everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files that must not be touched by the text filter.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
